exec
Usage: exec [COMMAND [ARG]...]

Replace the shell process with COMMAND, keeping the same PID.

A shell builtin: there is no fork and no return. With no command, apply
its redirections to the current shell instead.

xos's init ends with `exec /bin/sh`, so the shell becomes PID 1 rather
than a child of it.

	exec 3<&0	open fd 3 as a copy of stdin

See also: eval, exit
